20260527.115526.974 [<ideas.........] [Now I have a clear understanding of the formal system.]
20260527.115527.188 [<ideas.........] [The package `enn` uses lazy imports and its API has shifted to an `ENNStatefulFitter` pattern with `tell` and `ask` methods,]
20260527.115527.389 [<ideas.........] [while `enn_fit` is now internal and `enn_fit.py` only includes `subsample_loglik`. The notebook still works with `from enn]
20260527.115527.567 [<ideas.........] [import EpistemicNearestNeighbors, enn_fit` but `enn_fit` is not exported from the package's `__init__`.]
20260527.115527.721 [<ideas.........] [To meet MBC2's request, three structurally distant ideas within the same formal system would be:]
20260527.115527.887 [<ideas.........] [1. A version where imports are fully explicit instead of lazy, maintaining notebook compatibility but removing dynamic]
20260527.115527.916 [<ideas.........] [attribute access.]
20260527.115528.014 [<ideas.........] [2. An extreme case where `ENNStatefulFitter` becomes purely functional with no state mutation, requiring all operations to]
20260527.115528.032 [<ideas.........] [be pure functions.]
20260527.115528.111 [<ideas.........] [3. An asymptotic edge case where the system operates at maximum entropy or minimum information gain, effectively making]
20260527.115528.146 [<ideas.........] [predictions indistinguishable from random noise.]
20260527.115528.291 [<ideas.........] [The core assumptions to challenge include the belief that the fix must reside within the package itself, that the notebook]
20260527.115529.087 [<ideas.........] [source is the ultimate authority, and that imports occur at module load time. Additionally, it's assumed that `enn_fit` is]
20260527.115529.414 [<ideas.........] [strictly a function, that there is only one import site, and that runtime conditions mirror the development environment]
20260527.115530.659 [<ideas.........] [exactly.]
20260527.115530.823 [<ideas.........] [The `enn_fit` name must exist, so it could be shimmied under a different mechanism. Notebook cells execute as-is, so]
20260527.115530.890 [<ideas.........] [preprocessing could address this.]
20260527.115531.102 [<ideas.........] [One idea involves making `enn` a PEP 562 lazy module where `enn_fit` isn't in the mapping but is resolved via a custom]
20260527.115531.412 [<ideas.........] [import hook in `sitecustomize.py`used already for nbmake. This hook intercepts `import enn` subattribute access exclusively]
20260527.115531.575 [<ideas.........] [for notebook sessions. The extreme approach requires zero changes to `src/enn/__init__.py`, effectively negating the need to]
20260527.115533.071 [<ideas.........] ["fix the package."]
20260527.115533.199 [<ideas.........] [The public API need not consist of real Python objects within the package. Instead of modifying the library itself, the fix]
20260527.115533.360 [<ideas.........] [can be implemented entirely within the test infrastructure by using a preprocessor or AST rewriter to transform the import]
20260527.115533.488 [<ideas.........] [statement in notebooks before execution, leaving the original notebook artifact unchanged. This approach keeps the notebook]
20260527.115533.584 [<ideas.........] [cell text identical while altering how it runs during testing.]
20260527.115533.764 [<ideas.........] [This transformation allows for maintaining legacy notebook compatibility without changing the package's structure,]
20260527.115533.824 [<ideas.........] [effectively decoupling the execution environment from the source code. The notebook artifact remains frozen on disk, but the]
20260527.115533.953 [<ideas.........] [execution graph differs through preprocessing, enabling the use of `ENNStatefulFitter` patterns without modifying the actual]
20260527.115534.753 [<ideas.........] [package or its exports.]
20260527.115534.939 [<ideas.........] [The notebook execution environment may differ from the source code, so the `enn_fit` import can be made available as a]
20260527.115535.353 [<ideas.........] [callable module using a `types.ModuleType` subclass or callable module, allowing `from enn import enn_fit` to work while]
20260527.115537.543 [<ideas.........] [preserving the original notebook structure.]
20260527.115537.734 [<ideas.........] [The structurally distant approach avoids importing `enn_fit` directly by using a dynamic import in a hidden bootstrap cell]
20260527.115537.931 [<ideas.........] [injected by nbmake, with the notebook's first cell rewritten. The `enn_fit` signature is captured once and implemented]
20260527.115540.452 [<ideas.........] [within the `EpistemicNearestNeighbors.fit_hyperparameters()` method itself.]
20260527.115540.598 [<ideas.........] [Notebook compatibility can be maintained by either preserving the `enn_fit` import or modifying the notebook to use method]
20260527.115540.939 [<ideas.........] [calls like `model.fit(k=...)`. Since the goal is to keep the notebook working in terms of behavior and output rather than]
20260527.115541.063 [<ideas.........] [literal source code, the import issue can be resolved through creative solutions within the formal system.]
20260527.115541.105 [<ideas.........] [One approach involves leveraging the existing `sitecustomize.py` patching of Jupyter to intercept and resolve `enn_fit`]
